  "notes": "The matched 1919 Howard Crane rendering establishes the seven fluted-pilaster bays with arched fanlights and faux balconies. Parks Canada and Winnipeg’s municipal heritage survey describe the terra cotta garlands, heavy cornice and brick parapet. The venue and architect record the present canopy and service wing."
